drm: nvidia-aware color pipeline discovery and cost-based planner

Derived from the nvidia-drm color pipeline work in the local spicy tree
(smithay 401912a6, 650a3457, cee8872a, c5c2d494; niri 96c7e4a7);
knowledge only, no code reuse. Evidence and gates are recorded in
docs/color-pipeline-nvidia-plan.md.

Discovery records each pipeline's COLOR_PIPELINE enum name (the only
stable vendor identifier; object ids shift between driver versions) and
qualifies 1D LUT interpolation by its current advertised value.

The greedy in-order matcher becomes a bounded cost-based DFS: a 1D LUT
can synthesize a decode curve the pipeline's curve ops lack (nvidia
offers only the PQ 125 pair), folding a following multiplier while the
decoded range fits [0,1] and leaving the rest pending for a later
multiplier or matrix; unused non-bypassable matrix/multiplier/LUT ops
are programmed to identity; a non-bypassable curve rejects the plan.
Fewest LUTs wins, so named curves stay preferred.

Format effectiveness follows the nvidia display engine: FP16 framebuffers
exclude the non-FP pipelines (their input-LUT ops fail atomic check) and
leave the leading FMT matrix inert. On 620.73.04 the FP pipelines were
reshaped (FP Lite is FMT-only), so FP16 transforms resolve nowhere and
stay composited until FMT effectiveness or the FP Full round-trip pair is
pixel-verified.

nvidia-drm negotiates the capability only with the experimental
AQUEOUS_DRM_COLOR_PIPELINE_POST_BLEND=1 opt-in; without the post-blend
encode path the capability would only disable implicit legacy YUV
scanout for no benefit. nouveau remains unqualified. Other drivers are
unchanged.

The FMT-inert assumption for FP16 is now switchable:
AQUEOUS_DRM_COLOR_PIPELINE_FP16_FMT=1 (drm_color_pipeline_set_fp16_fmt)
treats the leading FMT matrix as effective, letting gain-folded matrices
resolve on the FMT-only FP Lite pipeline. The default stays conservative:
an inert FMT silently drops the placed stage, so the assumption must be
pixel-verified before it can become a default.
